BT 14 TL 56 780 Td
/F2 15 Tf (Week 5. Why we need a model of quality of understanding) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Teachers often grade by counting: one mark for each correct point. Counting works for) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (facts, but it hides the difference between a student who lists ten disconnected facts) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (and a student who explains how three ideas depend on each other.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (To assess understanding we need a description of how learning outcomes grow in quality,) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (not only in quantity. The SOLO taxonomy provides such a description. SOLO means) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (Structure of the Observed Learning Outcome. It was proposed by John Biggs and Kevin) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (Collis in 1982 after analysing thousands of student answers in different subjects.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (The important words are "structure" and "observed". SOLO does not classify students or) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (their abilities. It classifies a particular answer: how many relevant aspects it) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (contains and how they are organised. The same student can give a relational answer on) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (one topic and a unistructural answer on another.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Because SOLO looks at the structure of an answer, it can be used in any discipline and) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (for written, oral and practical performance.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 290 40 Td (1) Tj ET
endstream
