/F2 15 Tf (Formative and summative assessment) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Summative assessment judges what has been learned at the end of a period. It produces a) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (grade that goes into the record. Formative assessment happens during learning and its) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (purpose is to improve learning while there is still time.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (The same task can serve both purposes. What makes assessment formative is the use of the) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (result: the information is used by the teacher to adapt teaching and by the student to) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (change how he or she studies.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Black and Wiliam \(1998\) reviewed a large number of studies and concluded that) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (strengthening formative assessment produces substantial learning gains, and that the) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (gains are often largest for students who were previously low achievers.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Formative assessment needs three things. Students must know the goal and the standard.) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (They must receive evidence about where their present performance stands in relation to) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (it. And they must have an opportunity to act on that evidence. Without the third) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (element, feedback is only a comment on the past.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (Practice tasks without grades in the record are valuable because students can show what) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (they do not understand without being punished for it.) Tj T*
